1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
wa alaikum wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuh, wa alaikum wa salam wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuh,

2
00:01:00,760 --> 00:01:04,480
Sallallahu alayhi wa alaihi wa sallam, Mubarakatuh.

3
00:01:05,540 --> 00:01:08,180
Our book on these days is Al-Adab al-Mufrat.

4
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:12,120
And we are about, we are discussing issues,

5
00:01:13,340 --> 00:01:17,100
expressions that are lawful for the Muslim to say,

6
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,720
and expressions that are not lawful.

7
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:26,120
Expressions that are lawful, but that some of the Muslims,

8
00:01:26,260 --> 00:01:28,460
they think that they are not lawful.

9
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:33,260
For example, yesterday we discussed Khosu Khuzakh.

10
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:37,820
Khosu Khuzakh, referring to the rainbow.

11
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:42,040
I'm sure we remember the rainbow we see on the sky.

12
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:43,460
We discussed this yesterday.

13
00:01:44,340 --> 00:01:52,080
Rainbows usually are a product of the twin process of reflection and refraction,

14
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:55,980
as we have come to understand from basic science.

15
00:01:56,980 --> 00:02:01,220
Arabs refer to the rainbow as Khosu Khuzakh.

16
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:08,420
Some of the scholars have mentioned that referring to the rainbow as Khosu Khuzakh,

17
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:11,600
is not a lawful expression.

18
00:02:13,220 --> 00:02:17,980
Some of the scholars say that referring to the rainbow as Khosu Khuzakh,

19
00:02:19,220 --> 00:02:22,020
is not an expression that is lawful.

20
00:02:23,020 --> 00:02:27,100
So, Imam al-Bukhari here in Al-Adab al-Mufrid,

21
00:02:27,640 --> 00:02:34,440
he seeks to affirm that using the expression Khosu Khuzakh.

22
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:39,740
Khosu means the arc, something that is curved,

23
00:02:40,940 --> 00:02:44,160
perhaps cuts an orange into two.

24
00:02:44,780 --> 00:02:50,140
One part of it is Khosu, that shape, that's curvedly shaped,

25
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:54,200
at the top, like the diameter of a circle.

26
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:59,100
If you cut a circle from the middle, or from any part of it,

27
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:03,400
even just cut across one point, across the other,

28
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:06,040
like obtaining a radius or something.

29
00:03:06,580 --> 00:03:09,540
If you obtain a radius, will you get an arc? No.

30
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:15,440
If you get a radius, will you get an arc? No.

31
00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:24,140
But if you get a diameter, the upper or the lower part of that diameter

32
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:28,200
will give you an arc. That arc is the Khos.

33
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:32,020
That's why the bow is also the Khos.

34
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:37,800
So, Arabs would refer to the rainbow as Khosu Khuzakh,

35
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:42,580
the arc or the bow of Khosakh.

36
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:47,680
So, it remains, what do they understand to mean Khosakh?

37
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:54,180
We have a Hadith that has come from the Prophet, alayhi salatu was salam,

38
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:59,780
that La Ta Kulu Kousa Khosakh, don't say Khosu Khosakh,

39
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:05,840
because Khosakh, Shayqanul, that word Khosakh,

40
00:04:05,980 --> 00:04:10,880
is the name of a devil or a demon amongst the jinns.

41
00:04:11,580 --> 00:04:16,680
But the ulama have established that that Hadith is Hadith al-Mawduh.

42
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:21,060
Like we said in class yesterday, al-Imam al-Albani discussed it

43
00:04:21,060 --> 00:04:25,680
in salat al-Ahadith al-Dha'ifa. The Hadith is not authentic.

44
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:30,560
To say that Khosakh refers to the name of a devil.

45
00:04:31,660 --> 00:04:35,580
In fact, in ancient Arabs, Arab literature,

46
00:04:35,580 --> 00:04:41,440
we also have it to say that Khosakh is the name of the idol

47
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:45,800
responsible for the rainbow itself, for the Khos itself.

48
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:51,380
All of these are narrations that are weak and unreliable.

49
00:04:52,420 --> 00:04:56,780
But because of these two things, some of the scholars have ruled

50
00:04:56,780 --> 00:05:00,090
that they don't say Khosu Khosakh, if Khosu Khosakh,

51
00:05:00,690 --> 00:05:06,510
if Khosakh refers to the name of a devil, or Khosakh refers

52
00:05:06,510 --> 00:05:10,990
to the name of an idol, they think it's responsible for the Khos.

53
00:05:11,310 --> 00:05:15,390
There is no lawful to say that, because the Khos belongs to Allah.

54
00:05:15,990 --> 00:05:18,550
So they say instead of saying Khosu Khosakh,

55
00:05:19,050 --> 00:05:23,630
you should say what Khosullah, the act that belongs to Allah.

56
00:05:23,630 --> 00:05:29,430
In fact, you can say Khosul Mator, the act of rain.

57
00:05:29,610 --> 00:05:33,090
Why? It is usually formed, of course, from physics.

58
00:05:33,450 --> 00:05:39,310
We understand that the rains come after, the rainbow come after,

59
00:05:39,650 --> 00:05:48,730
within some rainfall, since it's a joint result of a process

60
00:05:48,730 --> 00:05:50,210
of reflection and refraction.

61
00:05:50,210 --> 00:05:58,570
So you can say Khosu Khosakh, the act that becomes formed after rains.

62
00:06:00,430 --> 00:06:07,610
So, but a stronger linguistic and historic narration shows

63
00:06:07,610 --> 00:06:13,570
that the Arabs started to refer to the rainbow, the rainbow

64
00:06:13,570 --> 00:06:17,730
that we know as Khosu Khosakh, because the first times

65
00:06:17,730 --> 00:06:23,530
they noticed it, it was noticed around a mountain at Muzdalifa,

66
00:06:24,550 --> 00:06:26,090
called Jabal Khosakh.

67
00:06:27,230 --> 00:06:33,070
So it's like saying that Khos we saw around Khosakh mountain.

68
00:06:34,210 --> 00:06:40,370
That was one narrative about how it became to be called Khosu Khosakh.

69
00:06:41,070 --> 00:06:45,030
Another report said that it became called Khosu Khosakh,

70
00:06:45,630 --> 00:06:55,210
because Khosakh is from Taqzih, and Taqzih refers to At-tazyeen wa-tah-zeen.

71
00:06:55,610 --> 00:06:57,610
At-tazyeen is beautification.

72
00:06:58,470 --> 00:07:03,190
So the Khos, the act of the rainbow beautifies the sky.

73
00:07:03,990 --> 00:07:11,430
So it's like saying the act or that curve that beautifies the sky.

74
00:07:11,430 --> 00:07:17,770
We see that the various colors of the rainbow appears on the rainbow.

75
00:07:18,050 --> 00:07:22,550
So from the aspects of beautification, it was called Khosakh.

76
00:07:22,970 --> 00:07:26,790
And so it is lawful for us to say Khosu Khosakh.

77
00:07:27,190 --> 00:07:32,650
The entire discuss is about understanding what should we say,

78
00:07:33,470 --> 00:07:38,050
what should we should not say, what we can say, what we cannot say.

79
00:07:38,630 --> 00:07:43,530
In class yesterday, we also discussed the truth saying that

80
00:07:43,530 --> 00:07:50,010
Ya'lamu Allah or Allahu Ya'lamu Allah knows it,

81
00:07:50,310 --> 00:07:52,370
regarding something you are not sure about,

82
00:07:53,250 --> 00:07:55,650
or regarding something you don't even know about.

83
00:07:56,410 --> 00:07:57,770
Don't say Allah knows it.

84
00:07:58,610 --> 00:08:02,770
Something happens like we gave the example yesterday, one, two, three happened.

85
00:08:03,550 --> 00:08:04,890
So they asked you what happened?

86
00:08:04,890 --> 00:08:09,390
You said A, B, C, Allahu Ya'lamu, A, B, C happened.

87
00:08:09,630 --> 00:08:14,050
Ah, it means what you are saying is that what Allah knows was,

88
00:08:14,370 --> 00:08:18,710
regarding the matter A, B, C, you are ascribing A, B, C to Allah.

89
00:08:18,830 --> 00:08:22,230
When in reality what happened was one, two, three,

90
00:08:22,230 --> 00:08:29,810
meaning you are ascribing to Allah something different from what occurs in his knowledge.

91
00:08:29,810 --> 00:08:35,510
Like telling a lie and ascribing that lie to Allah Subhanahu wa Ta'ala.

92
00:08:35,690 --> 00:08:37,130
So that is not lawful.

93
00:08:37,890 --> 00:08:43,290
If you know something, yes, you can say this expression that

94
00:08:43,290 --> 00:08:47,450
Allahu Ya'lamu, if you know that is how it is,

95
00:08:48,530 --> 00:08:53,290
you want to affirm that what you have said is correct,

96
00:08:53,770 --> 00:08:55,370
and you know it to be correct.

97
00:08:56,170 --> 00:08:57,730
Al-Imamun Nawawi said,

98
00:08:58,030 --> 00:08:59,550
Falaa Ba'sa bi dhaliq.

99
00:08:59,550 --> 00:09:00,370
There is no blame.

100
00:09:01,110 --> 00:09:03,830
If you knew that the matter was one, two, three,

101
00:09:03,910 --> 00:09:09,190
and you are affirming that it is one, two, three, not correct.

102
00:09:10,310 --> 00:09:16,290
It is not inappropriate to say it is one, two, three.

103
00:09:17,410 --> 00:09:22,330
But if you don't know, don't say Allahu Ya'lamu,

104
00:09:22,930 --> 00:09:28,010
regarding something that you say, you have the answer to be wrong,

105
00:09:28,770 --> 00:09:33,710
and yet you are making Allah a witness over something you know to be wrong.

106
00:09:34,590 --> 00:09:39,190
Likewise, when you don't know, you are not certain about what exactly was the matter.

107
00:09:39,630 --> 00:09:45,610
Don't make Allah a witness or ascribe the knowledge of,

108
00:09:45,610 --> 00:09:49,770
to the knowledge of Allah, something you are not sure of.

109
00:09:49,770 --> 00:09:53,690
In fact, for us itself, even without an ascription,

110
00:09:54,750 --> 00:09:59,850
have we not been prohibited in the Qur'an, from saying what we don't know?

111
00:10:04,290 --> 00:10:06,510
Don't say what you don't know about,

112
00:10:07,430 --> 00:10:12,110
because Allah will ask you about what you say as Allah mentioned in Surah Al-Turk.

113
00:10:12,130 --> 00:10:14,870
Don't say what you don't know about.

114
00:10:15,210 --> 00:10:17,230
If you don't know, say, I don't know about it.

115
00:10:17,910 --> 00:10:22,210
Similarly, when a learned person is asked a question of knowledge,

116
00:10:22,410 --> 00:10:24,370
if he does not know, he should say, I don't know.

117
00:10:24,690 --> 00:10:27,090
La adil, la adil.

118
00:10:27,810 --> 00:10:30,390
But when you don't know, you say Allahu Ya'lamu.

119
00:10:30,430 --> 00:10:32,510
Many of the scholars say, no, don't say that.

120
00:10:32,670 --> 00:10:35,290
If you don't know, say la adil, la adil.

121
00:10:35,410 --> 00:10:40,510
But if you know, after full explanations and all of these,

122
00:10:41,190 --> 00:10:44,590
you cap it all up by saying Allahu Ya'lamu,

123
00:10:44,590 --> 00:10:48,590
by way of humbling yourself, by way of affirming

124
00:10:48,590 --> 00:10:51,190
that absolute knowledge of every matter,

125
00:10:52,070 --> 00:10:54,670
comprehensive knowledge of every matter,

126
00:10:55,170 --> 00:11:00,330
having and encompassing understanding of every matter belongs to Allah,

127
00:11:00,810 --> 00:11:01,970
then that is correct.

128
00:11:02,630 --> 00:11:11,410
So, you can see that our Deen Islam places a lot of emphasis on things we say.

129
00:11:11,410 --> 00:11:17,470
And you say this, or you should not say this.

130
00:11:18,810 --> 00:11:23,750
When yesterday, we referred to Sheikh Bakr ibn Abi Zaid,

131
00:11:24,330 --> 00:11:28,250
who was saying and affirming that what al-Imam al-Bukhari did here,

132
00:11:28,850 --> 00:11:36,250
by telling us that Babu Qawsu al-Quzah al-Babun Qawsu al-Quzah,

133
00:11:36,250 --> 00:11:41,850
is to affirm that it is lawful to say Qawsu al-Quzah regarding the rainbow.

134
00:11:42,650 --> 00:11:50,190
We referred to his book Mu'jumu al-Mana'i al-Lafziyah.

135
00:11:50,410 --> 00:11:54,750
That book is a very big book, very big.

136
00:11:55,510 --> 00:12:01,830
More than 500 pages, more than 600 pages.

137
00:12:02,570 --> 00:12:09,310
And all that it was talking about, things that we can say, things that we cannot say.

138
00:12:10,210 --> 00:12:17,730
It means there is a lot of emphasis in our religion regarding Hibzul-Islam,

139
00:12:18,110 --> 00:12:23,030
watching what you say, being certain what you say.

140
00:12:23,150 --> 00:12:28,250
Can I say this as a Muslim? Should I not say this as a Muslim?

141
00:12:28,250 --> 00:12:33,230
From the things that we studied yesterday, it's about Al-Majarra.

142
00:12:33,390 --> 00:12:40,230
Al-Majarra now, it's a technical word amongst the Arabs to refer to the Milky Way.

143
00:12:41,270 --> 00:12:45,690
But in the earlier times, the early Muslims described Al-Majarra.

144
00:12:45,930 --> 00:12:53,590
Yes, the word can be used, words in technical usage can be borrowed from linguistic usage.

145
00:12:53,590 --> 00:13:00,830
It can be borrowed from linguistic understanding and employed for modern-day use technically.

146
00:13:00,930 --> 00:13:03,090
Even in English language, that one occurs.

147
00:13:03,630 --> 00:13:06,570
Look at that word. I usually make an example with it.

148
00:13:06,570 --> 00:13:08,150
F-O-R-C-E, force.

149
00:13:09,250 --> 00:13:11,710
In language, it means you cannot compel me to do something.

150
00:13:12,530 --> 00:13:17,950
You cannot push me. You cannot push me in any way, whether physically or mentally.

151
00:13:18,870 --> 00:13:23,150
Pushing the person and making him do it.

152
00:13:23,710 --> 00:13:27,510
That is force against his will anyway.

153
00:13:28,870 --> 00:13:34,170
So, but today it is employed in physics and in fact in chemistry.

154
00:13:35,590 --> 00:13:39,330
The way it is even used in both science may be different slightly.

155
00:13:41,030 --> 00:13:45,190
The way it may be used in both may be slightly different.

156
00:13:46,010 --> 00:13:49,090
So you say force, you want to push something from the ground.

157
00:13:49,970 --> 00:13:53,570
It is there originally. That thing has an original inertia.

158
00:13:54,190 --> 00:13:55,570
It does not want to move.

159
00:13:56,030 --> 00:14:03,850
You need a force that is above the weight of that object for that object to move.

160
00:14:05,030 --> 00:14:08,450
So that is that you are compelling it to move against its will.

161
00:14:08,450 --> 00:14:17,370
It will now move when your employed force is bigger than its own resistance.

162
00:14:18,230 --> 00:14:21,670
As if to say you made him to move against his will.

163
00:14:22,190 --> 00:14:30,690
But when the will not to move is lower than the force to move, then it will move.

164
00:14:31,550 --> 00:14:33,910
So you can see this understanding was brought.

165
00:14:33,910 --> 00:14:41,230
And then force, forcing somebody to do something, we began to ascribe units to it in science.

166
00:14:41,810 --> 00:14:43,730
So the same thing Al Majarrah.

167
00:14:44,030 --> 00:14:50,350
Majarrah refers to a huge calabash looking structure inside the sky.

168
00:14:50,450 --> 00:14:58,050
Far away from which water poured from the skies, like a gateway to the sky.

169
00:14:58,170 --> 00:15:02,830
It was far away. So they used to consider it as a gateway into the heavens.

170
00:15:03,790 --> 00:15:13,750
But today Al Majarrah, most literal translators will refer to Al Majarrah as the Milky Way.

171
00:15:13,850 --> 00:15:21,630
And we know what it means. The Milky Way is the world of gases far away.

172
00:15:22,330 --> 00:15:27,090
World of gases far away from us. So far away.

173
00:15:27,930 --> 00:15:38,410
So words can be used in one form at a particular generation and in another generation it is used in another form.

174
00:15:38,610 --> 00:15:44,690
In all of that we want to know what is lawful for us to say as Muslims.

175
00:15:45,250 --> 00:15:50,370
What is not lawful? What is discouraged? What is encouraged?

176
00:15:50,370 --> 00:15:55,050
In fact, in some cases during Ibadat what is compulsory?

177
00:15:55,470 --> 00:16:00,070
Like the recitation of Surat al-Fatiha when we are in Salah.

178
00:16:01,190 --> 00:16:09,810
So this is just a recap of the entirety of our lesson for the past few weeks till we had the class yesterday.

179
00:16:10,570 --> 00:16:17,190
As I speak I would like to obtain a permission to leave the class.

180
00:16:17,890 --> 00:16:21,150
And by the will of Allah we can come back to class next week.

181
00:16:23,530 --> 00:16:31,650
Or can we make it a QA session? Can we continue today in a QA session?

182
00:16:33,670 --> 00:16:40,590
Or we come back to class in the next week because I am very mentally occupied.

183
00:16:42,350 --> 00:16:52,030
Like we said we have a few questions. Can we take a few questions?

184
00:16:52,130 --> 00:16:57,830
We can take a few questions and stop on the dot of the time. We can do that too.

185
00:17:00,490 --> 00:17:07,210
The first question I can see here says, when we are praying during sujood,

186
00:17:08,550 --> 00:17:19,130
do we have to say, when we pray during sujood, do we have to say and repeat

187
00:17:21,510 --> 00:17:30,610
In every sujood, all the last Salawat during Atiyah and Tasha'ud suffice?

188
00:17:33,090 --> 00:17:40,370
In Salat, what we have been told to do in sujood basically is to say,

189
00:17:43,150 --> 00:17:49,670
In sujood, in Salat, the basic thing to say we must say,

190
00:17:52,750 --> 00:17:56,030
When we are in sujood, we must say,

191
00:18:03,030 --> 00:18:07,310
We can also say,

192
00:18:16,470 --> 00:18:21,030
Saying it once is absolutely compulsory.

193
00:18:22,030 --> 00:18:29,910
Saying these expressions at least once, the ulama say it is compulsory.

194
00:18:30,790 --> 00:18:36,300
But to say it twice and thrice are very strongly encouraged.

195
00:19:04,850 --> 00:19:13,910
So we are, as we explained.

196
00:19:14,660 --> 00:19:18,990
Now if the individual wants to say,

197
00:19:39,150 --> 00:19:43,370
Now if the individual wants to say,

198
00:19:44,730 --> 00:19:45,470
Now if the individual wants to say,

199
00:19:45,470 --> 00:19:54,570
Like the Prophet Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam encouraged us to make a lot of dua in our sujood.

200
00:19:54,630 --> 00:19:55,690
In fact he said,

201
00:19:59,170 --> 00:20:05,710
It is most very likely that you will be granted your request.

202
00:20:06,530 --> 00:20:09,790
You now want to make dua in your sujood. You make the dua.

203
00:20:09,790 --> 00:20:15,010
If it is Sallallahu Alaihi Nabi that you want to make, you make Sallallahu Alaihi Nabi.

204
00:20:15,790 --> 00:20:21,090
You know that is upon your choice now that you are making dua in your sujood.

205
00:20:21,950 --> 00:20:27,190
What may become an innovation is that you are doing that in the last sujood.

206
00:20:27,970 --> 00:20:30,050
And every day it's the last sujood.

207
00:20:31,130 --> 00:20:35,970
So that it becomes as if the last sujood is a sujood for extra dua.

208
00:20:36,310 --> 00:20:37,470
Don't do it like that.

209
00:20:40,010 --> 00:20:44,330
Don't particularize what the Sharia generalizes.

210
00:20:45,150 --> 00:20:50,510
Don't particularize what the Sharia generalizes.

211
00:20:51,090 --> 00:20:54,030
You can make your dua in any of the sujood.

212
00:20:54,910 --> 00:21:05,150
Now don't make it become as if the only time you can make your dua a sujood is when you are upon the last sujood.

213
00:21:05,850 --> 00:21:11,070
But if you want to make dua in sujood, you can make Sallallahu Alaihi Nabi.

214
00:21:11,530 --> 00:21:20,650
If you want to make dua in all the eight sujood of a four raka'ah Sallah, yes you can make Sallahu Alaihi Nabi.

215
00:21:20,990 --> 00:21:26,670
Don't forget that is if you are praying alone or you are leading the people in prayer.

216
00:21:27,250 --> 00:21:30,450
Don't also forget if you lead the people in prayer

217
00:21:30,450 --> 00:21:35,430
and you want to so prolong your Sallah making dua in the sujood.

218
00:21:35,490 --> 00:21:46,450
Don't forget that the people behind you have a right to have the Sallah not so long becoming a difficult thing upon them.

219
00:21:46,870 --> 00:21:48,350
So don't forget their rights.

220
00:21:48,910 --> 00:21:53,530
But if you are upon your own nawafil, you are upon your own nawafil,

221
00:21:53,690 --> 00:21:58,170
then say Sallahu Alaihi Nabi in every sujood, there is no blame at all.

222
