494
00:46:43,710 --> 00:46:50,770
Can a female put ring in the ring finger, or the prohibition is for both gender?

495
00:46:51,610 --> 00:46:56,230
The prohibition is for males. We discussed this earlier. The women,

496
00:46:59,070 --> 00:47:11,030
the woman, she was knotted. All her life is about, is about adornment. But the woman can

497
00:47:11,030 --> 00:47:26,210
put the ring on all the fingers. The prohibition is regarding males, insha'Allah. I hope that it

498
00:47:26,850 --> 00:47:32,890
now. What are the two fingers that a male can use to wear the ring?

499
00:47:34,190 --> 00:47:41,950
We said it during that explanation, the small finger and the thumb. But what the

500
00:47:41,950 --> 00:47:50,870
Prophet used himself, because the Prophet wore rings too. There was a time he took a ring.

501
00:47:51,510 --> 00:47:59,450
Al-Imam al-Tirmidhi mentioned that in his Shama'il Nabi, it's an entire book about the Prophet's

502
00:47:59,450 --> 00:48:06,290
personal conduct in his day-to-day life. The day-to-day personal conduct of the Prophet,

503
00:48:06,810 --> 00:48:12,190
alayhi salatu was-salam. One of the things mentioned about him was that he had a ring

504
00:48:12,190 --> 00:48:20,590
at a point in time. That ring was made from silver. The ring of the Prophet is not gold.

505
00:48:20,590 --> 00:48:29,230
Wearing gold is haram. So the ring was made for males. Wearing gold is haram for males.

506
00:48:30,750 --> 00:48:37,910
It's allowed for women if it is properly worn. But for the males, what we can wear is the silver.

507
00:48:39,130 --> 00:48:44,710
So the Prophet wore, alayhi salatu was-salam, it took a silver ring at a particular time.

508
00:48:45,670 --> 00:48:53,210
And that ring had a black, is it Onyx or Chalcedony? The black mineral at the middle.

509
00:48:54,210 --> 00:49:03,590
That was the head of the ring. And it had Muhammad Rasulullah on it. Allah was on top.

510
00:49:04,290 --> 00:49:12,790
Rasul was at the middle. Muhammad is under, below it. So you see Muhammad, you read it from below,

511
00:49:12,790 --> 00:49:23,970
up, Muhammad, down most word, Rasul, above it, then Allah above it. So this was how the ring of the

512
00:49:23,970 --> 00:49:31,550
Prophet was, alayhi salatu was-salam. He used to make it as a stamp for his letters. When he wrote

513
00:49:31,550 --> 00:49:39,170
a letter, he placed the ring and then he stamped it. So this ring, it was with Abu Bakr and Siddiq.

514
00:49:39,170 --> 00:49:44,890
I think it got lost with Uthman Ibn Affan. So the Prophet took,

515
00:49:45,110 --> 00:49:51,890
salallahu alayhi was-salam, a ring, a silver ring, and he was wearing that ring on his small finger.

516
00:49:52,710 --> 00:49:58,810
So men should wear the rings on the small finger. If you are following the Sunnah by wearing the

517
00:49:58,810 --> 00:50:05,330
ring, you wear the ring on the small finger. But if it is just that you are just doing your own,

518
00:50:05,330 --> 00:50:11,770
then you may not earn rewards for it. So wear the ring on the small finger. As for the tomb,

519
00:50:11,930 --> 00:50:16,630
even though there is no prohibition about it. So if you wear a ring on the tomb as a man,

520
00:50:17,210 --> 00:50:22,870
we don't have a reason to prohibit you. We don't have a proof to say, oh no, don't.

521
00:50:24,390 --> 00:50:30,490
But the Sunnah is that wear the ring on your small finger. As for the first finger, the second

522
00:50:30,490 --> 00:50:36,210
finger, and the ring finger, the ulama prohibit it. And there are reports regarding that from the

523
00:50:36,210 --> 00:50:41,090
Sunnah too, especially for the first finger and the middle finger. The ring finger,

524
00:50:41,310 --> 00:50:47,710
that's a prohibition from the scholars because they connect it to At-Tasha Buhubi Kufar,

525
00:50:47,950 --> 00:50:55,730
behaving like Kufar, who choose wearing rings to be on the ring finger, because they believe that

526
00:50:56,270 --> 00:51:02,230
that connects the heart from that finger. So when you put a ring on it during marriage,

527
00:51:02,850 --> 00:51:09,650
the ring helps you to sustain your marriage. So we avoid that. They do it for worship. We avoid

528
00:51:09,650 --> 00:51:15,610
behaving like them. So that who sees us does not think that we also have that belief they have.

529
00:51:16,730 --> 00:51:21,190
So don't put rings on your first three fingers, the first finger, the middle finger,

530
00:51:21,190 --> 00:51:26,770
and the ring finger. You can put your ring on the thumb, but the Sunnah is that you have your ring

531
00:51:26,770 --> 00:51:34,430
on the small finger. For men, as for women, put the ring wherever you want. If you like,

532
00:51:34,470 --> 00:51:40,350
put all the fingers, put ring there, right, put ring left, ten fingers, ten rings.

533
00:51:41,270 --> 00:51:46,250
For a woman, there is no blame, inshallah. I hope that this is clear by Yusuf.

534
00:51:51,330 --> 00:51:52,030
Amin.

535
00:51:54,410 --> 00:51:59,150
There is a mosque where they are not completely facing the Qibla,

536
00:51:59,510 --> 00:52:05,650
such that only the Imam has to bend in order to face the Qibla properly. Is this solid valid?

537
00:52:08,070 --> 00:52:15,490
Not facing Qibla now has misconceptions. Many times when this expression is employed,

538
00:52:16,450 --> 00:52:24,190
people have misconceptions about it. Not every deviation counts as not facing the Qibla. Is

539
00:52:24,190 --> 00:52:31,450
this clear? Not every deviation, every slight deviation from the Qibla. You now say, no,

540
00:52:31,450 --> 00:52:38,740
it's not facing the Qibla. No, not every deviation counts as not facing the Qibla.

541
00:52:39,980 --> 00:52:46,100
Because the Qibla is a direction, not a point. Please let us, that's the second rule.

542
00:52:47,100 --> 00:52:53,280
The first rule regarding answering this question is that not every deviation counts as

543
00:52:53,280 --> 00:52:58,580
deviation in terms of the Qibla. Some does not count. It may be deviating, but it does not count.

544
00:52:59,020 --> 00:53:04,220
It does not count as from the things that will invalidate Yusuf. It does not count to say you

545
00:53:04,220 --> 00:53:10,380
deviated from the Qibla. You are still within the range of the Qibla. That brings us to the

546
00:53:10,380 --> 00:53:18,100
second basic rule that the Qibla is a direction and not a point. The meaning is that it has a

547
00:53:18,100 --> 00:53:24,220
wide range. If you are an architect or an engineering person, you understand what I mean.

548
00:53:24,640 --> 00:53:32,780
The difference between facing a point and facing a direction. There is a big difference between

549
00:53:32,780 --> 00:53:38,940
facing a point and facing a direction. The Qibla is a direction and not a point.

550
00:53:40,060 --> 00:53:40,840
Because Allah says,

551
00:53:41,120 --> 00:53:44,700
فَوَلُّ وُجُوهَكُمْ شَطْرَ الْمَزْجِدِ الْفَرَامِ

552
00:53:44,700 --> 00:53:49,580
Shatra there means in the direction of Masjid al-Haram.

553
00:53:51,220 --> 00:53:53,500
فَوَلُّ وُجُوهَكُمْ شَطْرَحَمِ

554
00:53:53,500 --> 00:53:59,560
This shatru is direction. So and then he said in that hadith of Abu Hurairah that

555
00:54:00,380 --> 00:54:02,180
فَوَلُّ وُجُوهَكُمْ شَطْرَحَمِ

556
00:54:02,180 --> 00:54:06,640
So between the east and the west is the Qibla. It means the Qibla is a direction.

557
00:54:07,560 --> 00:54:12,900
It is not a point. If you understand this very well, I'm sure the issue will be simple.

558
00:54:13,180 --> 00:54:20,760
So it's not every change, every slight change that counts as a change of a direction.

559
00:54:21,840 --> 00:54:27,180
So in that case, sometimes the imam may be slightly bent. You are not slightly bending

560
00:54:27,740 --> 00:54:33,020
and you have not moved away from the Qibla. The imam has not also moved away from the Qibla.

561
00:54:33,060 --> 00:54:40,420
You have not moved away from the Qibla. Why? That slight bending is within the range of acceptance.

562
00:54:41,460 --> 00:54:47,140
The slight bending is within the range of acceptance. So if it is within the range of

563
00:54:47,140 --> 00:54:53,000
acceptance, then you have Salah. Both the imam and the rest of the people, you have your Salah.

564
00:54:53,000 --> 00:54:59,840
The Salah is valid. I hope that this is clear by Yusuf. But if it is not within

565
00:55:00,360 --> 00:55:06,180
the range of acceptance, such that we can say you are not facing this direction,

566
00:55:06,980 --> 00:55:14,840
you are completely away from the direction, then in that case, if they had done it deliberately,

567
00:55:15,820 --> 00:55:20,160
knowingly, they knew that this is not the direction of the Qibla and yet they faced it,

568
00:55:20,160 --> 00:55:23,420
they don't have Salah. The Salah is invalid.

569
00:55:25,320 --> 00:55:32,620
Because one of the shurus of Salah is the Qibla. The Qibla must be faced.

570
00:55:33,640 --> 00:55:37,620
And that's what we read. It occurs in the Qur'an about two or three times,

571
00:55:37,840 --> 00:55:44,800
face the Qibla, face the Qibla, face the Qibla. But it's a short, it's a short two for Salah too.

572
00:55:44,800 --> 00:55:49,120
But if it's that they did not know, they were trying to find the Qibla,

573
00:55:49,220 --> 00:55:54,240
study, do this, and then they ended up observing the Salah, and then later found that

574
00:55:54,240 --> 00:55:59,640
where they had faced for that Qibla was not the correct Qibla, then the Salah is valid.

575
00:56:01,680 --> 00:56:09,090
That is now when you say for Aynama tuvalu fattam mawajhullah. I hope that it is clear by Yusuf.

576
00:56:15,340 --> 00:56:18,040
And we quality be here now.

577
00:56:23,160 --> 00:56:25,640
